A||||3||ThatRickGuy||Where do I put the thermometer?||||1||
Z||000000||ThatRickGuy||06-16-2000||09:05 AM||||Hey guys, When I picked up my fiero, the prior owner told me that the temp guage doesn't work, but the idiot light for temp does. Are these 2 warning systems both for coolant temp? are they both run off the same sender? I'm trying to figure out if I just need to replace the sending unit, or if I need to start looking for a set of guages.<P>Thanks<BR>-Rick||||reg||1
Z||000001||lennyb4||06-16-2000||10:02 AM||||Ummmm..Where to put the thermometer???? hehehehehehehehe...im leaving this one alone  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000002||StuGood||06-16-2000||10:49 AM||||If yours is a V6, sending unit is on LHS, aft corner of rear cyl. head.  2-pin connector - frequently crumbles away from heat damage.<P>To test wiring+ idiot light, turn ignition key on, briefly ground each of the 2 wires on the harness that go to the sending unit.<P>When you ground one wire, idiot light should light.  Ground other wire and temp gage should peg. ||||reg||3
Z||000003||ThatRickGuy||06-16-2000||04:02 PM||||Lenny, the subject was ment jokingly, I was attempting to be humorous, still awaiting the "tail pipe" responce...<P>Stu, Good call on the testing, I've been running a little braindead lately.<P>||||reg||1
